  <div class="subsection-heading">Priority area 2 – ST2</div>
  <p>This area is highly influenced by the coal storage practices at the power plant (Figure 3). It also has a substantial amount of impervious area (64%). Particulates and TSS are the key pollutants of concern in this area. Several opportunities exist to address this hot spot.</p>
  <p><strong>Recommendation</strong></p>
  <p>Construct a covered facility for coal storage and handling.</p>
  <p>Retrofit the parking lot adjacent to the Liturgical Press to provide a vegetated filter strip, treating the overland discharge of pipe flow at this location.</p>

  <div class="subsection-heading">Priority area 3 – GE1</div>
  <p>This sub-sewershed has the largest annual pollutant load of the 18 outfalls, almost four times the average load for the campus. The estimated annual TP input to East Gemini from GE1 is 22.6 pounds, one-sixth of the total annual TP load contributed by the wastewater</p>

